From f15df25b7b164399fc6b6db5359bb9cb2e44b1c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:52:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: do a full modeset when colour management changes
 the DSPP need

A colour-management change that adds or removes the CTM or the gamma
LUT (GNOME Night Light switching on or off, a colour profile being
loaded or dropped) changes the number of DSPP blocks the CRTC needs.
The DSPPs are assigned together with the mixers, and the change only
reaches the hardware cleanly through a full modeset.

Set mode_changed in dpu_crtc_check_mode_changed() when the DSPP need
changes. A change of the CTM / LUT values alone (the Night Light ramp)
keeps the fast colour-only path, so the panel is not re-enabled for
every step.

Based on tb323fu-linux 0079 (Joonhoe Kim, "drm/msm/dpu: keep the full
modeset when colour management changed"), which keeps mode_changed set
in that project's in-place VFP path (their 0065, not carried here); the
same intent is moved to the place where this tree decides on a modeset.

Link: https://github.com/joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux (kernel/patches/0079)
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
index 0e4f2fd0a8..082c8c7dfc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -1509,6 +1509,11 @@ static int dpu_crtc_assign_resources(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool dpu_crtc_needs_dspp(const struct drm_crtc_state *state)
+{
+	return state->ctm || state->gamma_lut;
+}
+
 /**
  * dpu_crtc_check_mode_changed: check if full modeset is required
  * @old_crtc_state:	Previous CRTC state
@@ -1536,6 +1541,16 @@ int dpu_crtc_check_mode_changed(struct drm_crtc_state *old_crtc_state,
 	    (!clone_mode_requested && clone_mode_enabled))
 		new_crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * A colour-management change that adds or drops the CTM / gamma LUT
+	 * changes the number of DSPPs the CRTC needs; they are (re)assigned
+	 * with the mixers, so do a full modeset in that case. A change of the
+	 * values alone (e.g. a Night Light ramp) keeps the fast path.
+	 */
+	if (new_crtc_state->color_mgmt_changed &&
+	    dpu_crtc_needs_dspp(old_crtc_state) != dpu_crtc_needs_dspp(new_crtc_state))
+		new_crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
-- 
